---
import StatePage from '../layouts/StatePage.astro';
import StateDirectory from '../components/StateDirectory.astro';
import { documentPages } from '../data/sitePages';
const faqs = [
 { question: 'What does a document bundle cost?', answer: 'The supported mechanics lien bundles and Florida Notice to Owner preparation tool cost $24.99 per purchase. Recording, postage, service, and attorney fees are separate.' },
 { question: 'Is an account required?', answer: 'No. Enter project information, review the preview, and use the hosted checkout. Keep the same browser available for the post-payment download.' },
 { question: 'Does the purchase file or serve my document?', answer: 'No. Preparation and download do not record a lien, deliver statutory notices, or begin a lawsuit. You are responsible for those steps and for reviewing legal requirements.' },
];
const schema = JSON.stringify([{ '@context':'https://schema.org', '@type':'WebSite', name:'MechanicsLienForm', url:'https://mechanicslienform.com/' }, { '@context':'https://schema.org', '@type':'FAQPage', mainEntity:faqs.map(f => ({ '@type':'Question', name:f.question, acceptedAnswer:{ '@type':'Answer', text:f.answer } })) }]);
---
<StatePage title="Mechanics Lien PDF Preparation Tools — $24.99" description="Prepare a mechanics lien PDF for seven supported states or a Florida Notice to Owner for $24.99. Read state guides, preview your details, and download." canonical="https://mechanicslienform.com/" schema={schema}>
 <section class="bg-navy-900 text-white"><div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 py-16 sm:px-6"><h1 class="max-w-3xl text-4xl font-bold sm:text-5xl">Turn your project records into a mechanics lien PDF</h1><p class="my-6 max-w-3xl text-xl text-blue-100">Choose a supported preparation tool, review your project details, and download your document bundle after payment. $24.99 per purchase. No account required.</p><a class="inline-block rounded-lg bg-white px-6 py-3 font-bold text-navy-900" href="/mechanics-lien/#paid-tools">Choose a paid tool</a><a class="ml-4 inline-block py-3 underline" href="#states">Read your state guide</a></div></section>
 <article class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 py-12 sm:px-6 prose prose-lg max-w-none">
 <h2>Know what you are buying before checkout</h2><p>MechanicsLienForm is a document preparation service. The mechanics lien workflow produces a claim draft and supporting deadline, filing, service, and release information. The available calculations depend on the state and facts entered; some deadlines need manual verification. Preview the information and check statutory forms, warnings, notice prerequisites, and county procedures before filing.</p>
 <p>The service does not verify the debt, search title, record documents, mail notices, or represent you in court. A recorder's acceptance does not establish that a lien is enforceable. Review disputed dates, contract tiers, residential protections, and required language with a construction attorney.</p>
 <h2>Three steps from records to download</h2><ol><li><strong>Gather your inputs.</strong> Use the <a href="/mechanics-lien/form/">form checklist</a> to organize ownership, property description, invoices, credits, contract parties, and furnishing dates.</li><li><strong>Review the preview.</strong> Compare every name, amount, and date with the source records. A state guide is useful for identifying missing notice or enforcement tasks.</li><li><strong>Pay and download.</strong> Complete checkout for the selected product. Keep your original browser available to generate the PDF and check email delivery. <a href="/contact/">Contact support</a> about a delivery problem.</li></ol>
 <h2 id="states">State guides and available tools</h2><p>Seven states currently offer mechanics lien preparation tools. The five additional state guides explain filing workflows without offering a state-specific lien download. Florida has a separate paid Notice to Owner tool. The cards identify availability.</p><StateDirectory />
 <h2>Choose the document for the task</h2><p>An early project notice, an unpaid-debt claim, a payment waiver, and a discharge of a recorded lien serve different purposes. Start with the guide for the task you need:</p><ul>{documentPages.map(p => <li><a href={p.path}>{p.name}</a></li>)}</ul>
 <h2>Purchase questions</h2>{faqs.map(f => <details class="rounded-lg border px-5"><summary class="cursor-pointer py-4 font-semibold">{f.question}</summary><p>{f.answer}</p></details>)}
 <p>Read <a href="/about/">about the service</a>, the <a href="/privacy-policy/">data handling policy</a>, and the <a href="/terms-of-service/">purchase terms</a> before entering sensitive project information.</p>
 </article>
</StatePage>